 Spatial items derive from COCO boxes. Each query supplies two to six same-category candidates $A$ and a single annotated reference instance $B$. One target lies on the requested side of $B$, with a center margin of 0.05 of the relevant image dimension and separation constraints; all distractor centers lie on the opposite side. Relations are left, right, above, and below in the image plane, not three-dimensional judgments. All non-crowd target-category instances must have annotation-area ratio at least 0.002 and box side lengths at least 24 pixels. Generation uses seed 0 and per-subset caps of 60 items per category and two per image. The spatial subset contains 527 queries from 375 images and 57 target categories. Its two box-area strata contain 233 target-largest and 294 target-not-largest items.
 
